# Treat source as text so git renders diffs even when files contain multibyte
# characters (em dashes, ×, ≥, etc.) that trip git's binary heuristic.
#
# `text` alone does NOT do that — it only controls end-of-line normalization.
# Git decides whether to render a diff by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8k,
# and `text` does not override that. `diff` does. This was learned the hard way:
# scripts/model-eval.ts used a raw NUL as a map-key separator, so every diff of it
# read `Bin 23178 -> 23417 bytes` and its changes were unreviewable. Setting `diff`
# means a stray NUL degrades to an ugly diff instead of no diff at all.
*.ts   text diff
*.tsx  text diff
*.js   text diff
*.jsx  text diff
*.json text diff
*.md   text diff
